// EXPECT: [E085]
// LAINFLAGS: --engine=ir-full
// SOUNDNESS PAIR for callsite_return_range_pass.ln. The binding is a GLOBAL channel consulted
// while seeding a callee's parameters, so the danger is one call site's intervals reaching a
// different call — or a different function entirely. Two guards make that impossible and both
// are exercised here:
//
//   · a nested UNBOUND query clears the channel before analysing, so a callee reached from
//     inside a bound analysis is still seeded from its DECLARED intervals
//   · the memo is restored afterwards, because a call-site answer is not valid everywhere
//
// `dbl(2)` above it is bindable and `dbl(k)` is not; if the tight answer leaked from the first
// to the second, `t[dbl(k)]` would be "proven" for an argument that can be anything.
func dbl(a i32) i32 { return a +% a }
func f(k i32) i32 {
    var t i32[8] = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
    var good i32 = t[dbl(2)]
    return good + t[dbl(k)]
}
func main() i32 { return f(1) }
